 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "I like to do something.",
   "texto": [
    "With **любить** + infinitive: **Я люблю читать** (I like to read), **я люблю гулять** (I like to walk), **я люблю путешествовать** (I like to travel).",
    "**Что ты любишь делать в свободное время?** = what do you like to do in your free time? **Свободное время** is «free time»."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Play and play: играть",
   "texto": [
    "In Russian is the same verb, **играть** (играю, играешь, играет), but changes the preposition and shape of the name.",
    "Sports and games, with **в + acusativo**: играть **в футбол**, **в теннис**, **в шахматы** (chess).",
    "Instruments, with **на + preposicional**: играть **на гитаре** (play guitar; гитара → гитаре)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Go often: ходить",
   "texto": [
    "To talk about an activity or a destination to which **habitualmente o repetidas veces** goes, **ходить** is used: хожу, ходишь, ходит. It does not necessarily mean that you go on foot: **ходить в спортзал** usually means «Go to the gym.».",
    "**Я часто хожу в кино** = I often go to the movies. **Я хожу в спортзал каждый день** = I go to the gym every day.",
    "**Идти** usually describes a specific path in a direction, in progress or planned; **ходить** expresses regular, repeated or back-and-forth movement. **Гулять** means walking or taking a walk."
   ]
  },
